## HONEST WEAKNESSES

1. FX conventions are NOT uniform across the costed rows. The six Chinese issuers' flow figures use the
   2025-12-31 period-end rate CNY 6.9961 (the HK worker's original current-spot conversions were
   renormalized to it from the RMB originals). Asahi's flows use a fiscal-year-average ~JPY 151.
   Glencore is USD-native. All differ from a strict fiscal-average basis; a USD figure may move 2-3%.
   Chokepoint ranking is unaffected. This is a method disclosure, not a sourcing gap.

2. verify_edges reaches a document naming BOTH parties for only 14 of 38 edges. The other 24 split three
   ways, none silent: (a) the 14 SEMCORP + BTR edges are tier 1 from those firms' own annual reports,
   which name customers in Chinese (宁德时代 = CATL, 贝特瑞 = BTR), so the English-matching verifier
   reports HALF although the naming sentence was read by hand; (b) four first-party sources (POSCO Future
   M -> GM, Li-Cycle -> GM, Redwood -> Volkswagen on the GM/VW newsrooms; Ganfeng -> Umicore) were
   unreachable at verify from bot-block or URL rot, kept per this repo's rot-is-not-death rule after the
   relationship was confirmed on the publisher's live site; (c) two greencarcongress tier-3 trade-press
   edges (Ganfeng -> Tesla, Ganfeng -> Volkswagen) were DEMOTED to gaps because that domain will not
   resolve from here and no first-party source replaced them. See gap-03-unreach-1..2.
   verify_sources tells the same story on the financials: 9 of 11 costed rows pass; the two failures are
   BTR and SEMCORP, whose Chinese-language filings name them 贝特瑞 and 恩捷 rather than their English
   roster names, so the matcher misses them although their revenue lines were spot-checked in the PDF by
   hand. Both figures stand; the citation resolves.

3. Eleven tier-4 (news-only) edges the workers produced were dropped at merge, which bars tier 4. Where a
   tier-1 source existed they were upgraded (the SEMCORP/BTR customer edges); the remaining nine are
   recorded as gap-03-tier4-1..9, not silent deletions.

4. The cell makers' own filings disclose supplier CONCENTRATION as percentages without names (CATL top
   five suppliers = a few percent each; BYD one customer > RMB 100bn, unnamed). So the largest anode and
   cathode flows INTO CATL and BYD are unmappable from the buyer side; the edges that exist come from the
   suppliers naming their customers. Recorded as gaps by the midstream worker (gap-03-matrec-*).

5. Umicore -> Envision AESC: the source names the counterparty only as "AESC"; binding it to Envision
   AESC is an inference (former NEC/Nissan AESC, now Envision-majority). Confidence medium.

6. Still foundation-thin next to 01: 19 of 30 companies uncosted, no timeseries, no politics lens.
